      "data": {
        "text": "**Initiating Code Generation**\n\nI'm currently focused on initiating the Python file structure for this text-to-speech project. My first step is to get `synthesize_text.py` operational, leveraging AWS Polly for the speech synthesis engine.\n\n\n**Structuring File System**\n\nI've made progress on the file structure; `synthesize_text.py` is underway, focusing on AWS Polly integration using `boto3`. I'm developing the `synthesize_text` function to handle text input and audio byte stream output. I'm also planning `speech_client.py` for client initialization and helper functions, along with `speech_models.py` for data structures. I will also create the remaining files, ensuring concrete external provider integration for each.\n\n\n**Expanding File List**\n\nI'm now expanding the file list, as I work on the project's foundational structure. After working on `synthesize_text.py`, I've started building `speech_client.py` and `speech_models.py` as initial helper files. Then I'll focus on the remainder: `synthesize_ssml.py`, `select_voice.py`, `save_audio.py`, `script_translate.py`, `script_safety.py`, `script_embedding.py`, and `tts_qa_transcript.py`, ensuring each uses a distinct external provider. For `synthesize_text.py` I'll incorporate a boto3 client for AWS Polly, ensuring the text-to-speech output is an audio byte stream. `speech_client.py` will handle client initialization, and `speech_models.py` will have the data structures. I will prioritize `speech_client.py`.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
